{
  "README": [
    "Shared pricing contract between the three engines that price a kitchen:",
    "the sales app (lib/features/viewer/models/cpq_engine.dart), the Studio",
    "(frontend/src/pricing.ts) and the office server (backend/catalog.py via main.price_quote).",
    "The salesperson quotes from the app; the client signs the PDF the server renders.",
    "If these ever disagree the client signs a different number than they were shown,",
    "so all three are checked against these figures, using the SAMPLE catalogue",
    "(assets/catalog/default_catalog.json) rather than any edited price list:",
    "  flutter test test/pricing_contract_test.dart",
    "  npm test --prefix frontend",
    "  python backend/test_pricing_contract.py",
    "Changing a rate or a rule means changing the sample catalogue AND the expected values here, deliberately.",
    "Wall work (openings with a `work` key, and `wall_finish`) is priced from the catalogue's wall_work, without the finish multiplier; the finish area is rounded to 0.01 m2 first.",
    "Expected values are worked out by hand, not copied from an engine's output."
  ],
